 "intro": {
  "@es": "Hoy aprendes a decir «me invitaron», «nos avisaron» o «lo respetan» sin nombrar a nadie. En ruso es muy frecuente usar el plural sin sujeto: no se dice quién actúa, pero el sentido es el de la pasiva.",
  "@en": "Today you learn to say «I was invited.», «We were warned.» or «They respect him.» without naming anyone. In Russian it is very common to use plural without subject: it is not said who acts, but the sense is that of passive."
 },
